nd u2 give reward 0, so there are long stretches with no dense progress signal. Rewards should be given for progress towards the subgoal within each state (e.g., a small positive reward for `has_door_key` in u1, `door_open` in u2) rather than only at the exact state-transitioning event. (7) The ordered-transition coverage is incomplete: there is no way to represent the valid sequence key-first-then-ball (u0 --has_door_key--> u1 --blocker_moved--> u2 --door_open--> u3), which is required by the environment mechanics. (8) FINAL_STATES header is present and u3 is declared and accepting, which is good, but the semantic gaps above prevent acceptance."}
